epartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 12,2 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,8, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,3 a 7,0. En diciembre se adjudicó el 3 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 6 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 55 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.500 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos, sino decisiones basadas en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. El límite legal no implica irregularidades por sí solo.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se ajustan a presupuestos cerrados o a demandas inmediatas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 59 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 12.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.3 to 7.0. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 55 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,500 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or genuine needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts [1] and [2] to ensure they align with the body's needs. Review the distribution of contracts across awardees to identify any unusual patterns. Look for repeated purchases from the same awardee to assess if they meet a specific requirement.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["XY73U4yfPO1%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D","6m4UprKdsyt9Zh%2FyRJgM8w%3D%3D","aIlXIzx5%2FECFlFRHfEzEaw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}